ower in combat a  seemingly  unattainable goal they want to reach an  iron determination to fight for that  goal as well as the ability to stick  through the toughest moments  you fight with the strength of many men  tonight  we see her fiercely and fearlessly  wielding a whole arsenal of cursed  weapons no matter how strong the  opponent she's facing and so i think  maki is so extremely likable because she  basically has all the characteristics  that our usual shonen hero has  only as a badass girl and supporting  characters to put this into perspective  she doesn't share any of the external  struggles and vulnerabilities that make  itadori so special and  does make it extremely easy to latch  onto her  something we for example see someone  like nobody this is someone  that stands up against the men who have  suppressed her entire life and fights  for becoming a powerful woman that can  lead the clan herself  basically her dream is showing everyone  that looked down on her  one big middle finger  so it's very easy to see what makes her  so extremely cool to watch and follow  other than megumi who internalizes the  pain caused by his family situation  maki displays her emotional damage  openly to the world  and yet i believe that the reasons maki  stands out as a character  as with any great character are the  underlying flaws  unseen symbols and steady character  progressions that happen beneath her  straightforward feeling surface  and gigiakutami sure went full out  when crafting her character  were born as twin sisters to the  powerful zane clan  the most powerful family in the jewish  two worlds  if it weren't for this guy right here  who basically carries the gojo family on  his own and as a result  maki's and my story isn't only dramatic  and sad in one way but  rather akutami has piled a whole  mountain of dramatic layers  on top of both of them that weighs down  heavily on their lives you know  just as american breakfast does first of  all there is the fact that the juju 2  world  operates based on very traditional and  conservative japanese rules  born into a powerful family you're  expected to always put the clan's  interests  first you have to be strong and flawless  serve your elders and bring no  shame onto the family name in other  words there is no room for  personal feelings and ambitions on top  of this  big surprise in this conservative combat  oriented and patriarchal family  structure  being born as a girl puts you on a harsh  disadvantage  right from the start you neither have  the same social standing nor the same  base physical strength of the male  family members  and so every woman has to work at least  twice as hard  to be recognized as a full-fledged  sorcerer  then there is the fact that maki and mai  are  twins which for a long time were seen as  a sign of misfortune in japan  i even found this very interesting study  that details different types of food  that pregnant japanese women were  supposed to avoid  to not bear twins such as twin chestnuts  double section tangerines or double  eggplants  thus being born a twin automatically  made you less worthy of love and trust  but as if all of this weren't enough  already maki and might actually  also have to deal with real physical  consequences of being twins as well  their cursed powers  basically treated them as one person as  well so that mai ended up with a  uniquely strong cursed ability but  no combat skills whatsoever while maki  is one of the physically  most gifted characters in the story but  without so much as an  ounce of cursed energy which in the  largest family of due to sorcerers  basically made her the worst among the  worst as a result  both maki and mai grew up as outcasts of  the same family which  left them with nothing but each other to  really hold onto emotionally  long story short maki and mai basically  both  share the same fate of growing up abused  and neglected by a family  that only cares about power and yet  both of them deal with it in very  different ways and while the story  introduces us to maki as the mature  tough and straightforward twin mai is  presented as hateful  evil and childish  and yet this perception is purposefully  misleading  as you might remember from my analysis  of nobara as we learned throughout their  flashback  in the relationship of the twins maki is  actually the more hurtful one  her big desire in life is paying back  those who abused her and her sister  who she always used to protect as a  child and yet  in the process of struggling to get  stronger she forgets about her sister  completely  focusing fully on her goal mai on the  other hand  never wanted to become a sorcerer in the  first place she  never had maki's mental strength for  that all she wanted was having her big  sister by her side  the only family she ever had and yet  through maki's struggle for  power she herself had no other choice  but also become a sorcerer  or be left alone at the bottom of the  [Music]  clan  in addition probably in an effort to  protect mai from the consequences of  going against the zane clan maki  severs her ties with her sister  completely however  this hurts mai even more and while she  can finally find comrades at the kyoto  school  she never had maki's conviction power or  drive  as a result we hear mai echoing a lot of  the opinions and behaviors of the people  around her as she doesn't have the  confidence to form her own opinions and  forge her own path  basically she's just letting herself be  pulled along by the stream of events  around her and  the only way she now sees to get her  sister's attention  is by taunting her or those around her  the place where she  actually wants to be ken  the point here is that very much in the  spirit of being twins  maki and mai are one person split into  two both dealing with their abusive  family  in their own way and yet at the same  time both  being a side of the same coin mai is  insecure  weak willed averse to fighting emotional  but also has an extremely powerful  ability that allows her to create  matter from nothing  and even though she actually forms  friendships really fast  her whole life is determined by her  relationship with her sister  her fault as a character then fault from  a writing perspective of course  is relying on maki and making her  responsible for her own feelings  and events in her life mice arc then is  about finding her own determination to  fight back against the abuse and  oppression by her family and the juju  two worlds  side by side with her sister maki on the  other hand  is strong a fighter and just like gojo  thinks everything can be done and solved  by strength alone  strength surely is important in the  jewish world marky has internalized a  very unhealthy view of strength  not showing any weakness as a result  maki blocks out her own emotions and  insecurities  completely focusing mostly on herself  similar to gojo she acknowledges the  value of having strong companions and  being able to fight together but in the  end her philosophy  is this  it's not that maki is a hateful person  it's that she's conditioned  not to accept any kind of love because  she was never  shown the unconditional love of a family  that she was owed she's so busy trying  to reject  everything that the zane clan stands for  that she can't really accept  other people's feelings at all positive  or negative  she's too busy thinking about herself  protecting herself  trying not to hate herself and so she  can't receive  mice feelings again i think it's really  easy to draw parallel to megumi here  who's not even blood related to his  sister  but does everything he can for his only  real family member  desperately wanting to talk to her  maki on the other hand who has the  chance to talk to her own twin sister  and  only real family in this world whenever  she wants  doesn't her having to wear glasses  because she otherwise is blind to curses  is really symbolic here because these  glasses  also represent her inability to see  other people for  who they are i think if you watched my  gojo video you will  recognize a pattern here  as a result maki's character arc is all  about understanding that strength  isn't always the answer and that forming  real relationships with others  especially her own sister is an  essential part of living a good life  and this also includes acknowledging and  accepting her sister's feelings and  wishes  into her heart and while her justified  hatred toward a family is a powerful  drive for her growth as a sorcerer  at some point after dealing with the  saiyan clan  she will need a more healthy goal in  life that is not defined by violence and  hate but that  actually will do good in the world or  sink  into deeper darkness as members of the  zayn family  sometimes tend to do zayn  one thing however is for certain maki  already being as strong as she is with  mai by her side once again becoming one  whole  she will be a force to be reckoned with  within the jewish world  and no one should underestimate her  power and role in the story  oh yeah sorry coming up next pure evil  why mahito is creeping you the [ __ ] out  go watch it here or any of these other  videos  thanks for watching peace

